# These sprites are stored as ordinary git blobs, not in LFS.
#
# The project's root .gitattributes routes *.png through LFS. That is the right default for
# the imported art -- 4K terrain and skybox textures are megabytes each. These are not that:
# eight generated shapes totalling about 25 KB, produced by HUDBuilder.cs and regenerable from
# it at any time.
#
# The reason to exclude them is that nothing in this repository is in LFS yet. Every PNG in
# HEAD is a plain blob, so committing these as pointers would make them the first objects to
# need an LFS endpoint on the remote -- a new dependency for the clone, the CI checkout and
# anyone who fetches without git-lfs installed, bought for 25 KB. A repository where some
# images silently need extra tooling and most do not is worse than either consistent choice.
#
# '!' unsets an attribute the root file's [attr]lfs macro set, rather than trying to override
# it with a different value.
*.png !filter !diff !merge -text
